  "title": "LoRA: 256 times fewer, and you can see it",
  "alt": "A hand-drawn whiteboard in which a densely hachured 4096 by 4096 square marked FROZEN with a padlock holds 16,777,216 parameters, while the LoRA detour beneath it is two slivers so thin they are drawn eight times thicker than true scale, meeting at a rank-eight waist and rejoining through a plus, with the arithmetic 32,768 plus 32,768 equals 65,536 and the ratio 256 circled. Below, a decaying singular-value spectrum recalls week 11, three bars compare 132.6, 21.3 and 14.2 GB against a 24 GB A10G line, and eight crossed-out full model copies are replaced by one base model with eight small adapter tabs clipped on.",
